  "adapter_contract": [
    "Construct request fields from literals, not a subject-generated signature. Compare returned decoded bytes/hash and accept/reject with these literal expectations.",
    "For each case, use literal seed_signature/chunk_signatures and payload profile, then apply wire_mutations without re-signing. Header variants already have independently re-signed literal signatures.",
    "Verify original writer header seed plus every data and zero MAC before forwarding an ordinary body signed with backend credentials and actual SHA256. Decoded quotas apply before backend mutation.",
    "Bound encoded bytes before read/allocation, decoded bytes before append, and all frames including zero. Exact length and end-of-stream prevent accepting a prefix.",
    "The model is non-trailer aws-chunked only. Unsupported trailers, additional chunk extensions and encodings reject explicitly.",
    "AWS minimum8192 for nonfinal data chunks makes1024 frames a defensive ceiling under1MiB; test its comparison with the valid3/2-frame boundary rather than invent tiny nonfinal chunks.",
    "Runtime authorizer must use actual request clock/credentials; tests evaluate the published2013 request at its own timestamp, without weakening freshness in runtime."
  ]
